content.text:
I inspected the repository. test/a_test.dart fails because lib/a.dart returns one less than expected; the fix and its test coverage split cleanly into an implementation task and a review task.

```json
{
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "t1",
      "title": "Fix off-by-one",
      "assignee": "codex",
      "prompt": "In lib/a.dart fix the off-by-one so that test/a_test.dart passes. Run `dart test test/a_test.dart` to verify; do not touch other files.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": "t2",
      "title": "Review and extend test",
      "assignee": "claude",
      "prompt": "Review the change in lib/a.dart, then extend test/a_test.dart with one edge case. Run `dart test test/a_test.dart` and make sure it passes.",
      "depends_on": [
        "t1"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "merge_instructions": "Run `dart test` and check `git diff --stat` only names lib/a.dart, lib/b.dart and test/a_test.dart."
}
```

